<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.7.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00961</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.7.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8e9d3ef9-93f0-43a1-91dc-ee599b7b6c73</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will work to find the slope of a line from two points, a graph, and a table. You will then use this knowledge to write equations of lines in three different forms: slope-intercept form, point-slope form, and standard form.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Write the slope of a line.</item>
  <item>Write the equation of a line in different forms.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>4.7.1: Evaluating Fractions</item>
  <item>4.7.2: Finding Slope From Tables, Graphs, and Points<list id="list-00003">
    <item>4.7.2: Self Check</item>
    <item>4.7.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
  
  <item>4.7.3: Writing Linear Equations <list id="list-00004">
    <item>4.7.3: Self Check</item>
    <item>4.7.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
 
  <item>4.7.4: Writing Equations From Two Points</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>4.7.5: Practice</item>
  <item>4.7.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list>
</section>
</content>
</document>
